Falsifies `block_roster_contract::read_is_total_and_every_counted_entry_is_gettable`.

The defect: `Roster::get` bounds its index with `i > self.count` instead of
`i >= self.count`, the off-by-one a reader writes when it thinks of `count` as a
last index. The entry one past the last is then fetched: it reads a slot the
writer never filled (or, on a page with no spare room, indexes past the entries
slice), so the roster claims a device that is not there.

Expected to fail: `assert!(roster.get(roster.len()).is_none())`, on any page the
header accepts, or an out-of-bounds slice inside `get` when the accepted page has
exactly `count` entries of room.


